How the components relate (no license propagation by linking)
-------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT body and the AGPL agents/pi/ component communicate only by spawning
separate processes and by local HTTP calls to an external worker. They are
separate programs aggregated in one repository, not a combined derived work,
so the AGPL does not propagate to the MIT-licensed adapters.

External programs interoperated with (no third-party code bundled here)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  * claude-mem worker  — Apache-2.0, a separately installed and run program
    that this project talks to over 127.0.0.1 HTTP. Not contained herein.
  * mem0                — Apache-2.0, a separately installed and run program
    reached over local HTTP. Not contained herein.
  * @mariozechner/pi-coding-agent / @mariozechner/pi-ai — peer modules
    provided at runtime by the pi agent; declared, never bundled.
  * DeepSeek Harness (dsh) / @deepseek-ai/dsh* — the runtime that hosts the
    Cordis plugin in agents/dsh/; provided by the dsh installation, never
    bundled.

